 389: **Theorem R7.3 (one-ply stop-criterion assembly) [Q3, PROVEN].** Fix one
 390: deterministic Defender policy which, at every
 391: reached epoch `P`, uses one actual pair `a in A_0(P)` satisfying
 392: `R_1(P,a)<=2`. If `M(P_0)<=2` at its root and such a choice remains available
 393: after every legal response on every reached history, then that same policy
 394: blocks forever.
