 517: ### 63.1 A residual-transversal condition
 518: 
 519: For a finite nonterminal Defender epoch `P`, define
 520: 
 521: ```text
 522: I_3(P)={W: W is alive at P and count_P(W)=3},
 523: tau_3(P)=the hitting number of {E_P(W): W in I_3(P)}.       (82)
 524: ```
 525: 
 526: The empty family has value zero, as usual. This is an initialization-only
 527: notation; it is not added to the proposed perpetual state invariant.
 528: 
 529: *Proof of Lemma L13.6.* Since `tau(P)=0` and every imminent residual is
 530: nonempty at a nonterminal epoch, `I(P)=empty`. Choose a transversal `X` of
 531: the alive count-three residuals with `|X|<=2`.
 532: 
 533: Every `x in X` is an empty cell of an Attacker-alive window and hence is
 534: legal by L6_2. If `|X|=2`, play its cells in axial lexicographic order. The
 535: second cell remains legal even if the first kills a label which formerly
 536: contained it, because it was already within distance five of an unchanged
 537: Attacker stone. If `|X|<2`, append sequential legal fillers using L1.2's
 538: finite max-`q` construction after the cells of `X` have been played.
