 506: At the three-anchor root, any Attacker response has at most two stones. If
 507: they share no window, there is no count-two label. If they are nonadjacent on
 508: one axis, any empty internal gap lies in every common window; if such a gap is
 509: already Defender-occupied, those windows are already dead. If they are
 510: adjacent, the two exterior flanks hit the five common windows, with any
 511: already-Defender-occupied or redundant flank omitted. Playing the needed
 512: cells first and then fillers deletes every count-two label, so the returned
 513: epoch has a candidate handoff with `L_23=empty` and exact `M=0`. This holds for
 514: every response and gives exact root `R_1=0` for every initial action.
